WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.304
The flow at this white point is a sum: one term from every particle.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.735
Start with the nearest particle. Its pink arrow is term m sub j.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.854
Add more, tip to tail. The terms shrink; solid teal is the running sum.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.952
Orange: the error of the first M terms, averaged over two hundred points.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.607
At sixteen terms, nineteen percent remains.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:31.420
Why so slow? Beyond rank sixteen, each term is tiny.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:37.404
But the eighty left over mostly align, and sum to a visible drift.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.451
A zero keeps only the M nearest.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:47.749
Eight terms: thirty-three percent error. Sixteen: nineteen. Thirty-two: eight percent.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.091
Each term lies in its own plane: offset and state.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:58.531
The flow is roughly the sum of the M nearest messages. Many small far terms add up to a drift.
